311 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Supplier bids or quotations may be solicited in a number of ways depending on the type and value of the intended purchase and the time frame available to make a purchase.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [13 14]
>>
endobj
312 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (a. Open- Invitation to all interested suppliers, invitation published in appropriate national publications or websites of the organization. Used for procurement of goods with a value exceeding Rs.500, 000or contracting of services above the value of Rs. 500,000. Donor thresholds may reduce these numbers. Will generally yield better pricing than Invitational bidding but requires a lot of time and preparation.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
313 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (b. Invitational- \(or Restricted\) Known suppliers contacted\(based on past performance quality and related factors\), low bid offer accepted. Along with negotiated procurement, this is the most commonly used for large- volume purchases. Generally, yields reasonable price offers, though it does take time for preparation and delivery and involves a moderate amount of work.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
314 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (C. Negotiated- A small number of potential vendors are approached, and specific price or service arrangements are directly negotiated. This method is most applicable to low- volume or emergency purchases. Prices may be less favorable though delivery times should be short.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
315 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (d. Direct- The simplest but usually the most expensive procurement method. Items are purchased from a single supplier at the quoted price. This should only be applicable to emergency purchases. Pricing may be unfavorable, but delivery times will be short, and the workload involved will be low.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
316 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (e. Sealed Bid- Used to preserve the integrity and fairness of supplier selection; will be used for all invitations for purchasesoverRs.50,000 for procurement of goods)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
